-- EXPECT-ERROR: `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` used in module `FieldCap` but `IO.FileWrite` is not declared in `needs`
-- `needs` coverage, TYPE DECLARATION positions (2026-08-05).
--
-- Check 1's decl walk visited `DFn` signatures, actor handler signatures and
-- extern cap types, then ended in a `| _ -> ()` wildcard — so a capability
-- named in a type DECLARATION was never looked at. This program typechecked
-- with exit 0, `--cap-strict` included, while declaring only `IO.Console`.
--
-- The module cannot OBTAIN a `Cap(IO.FileWrite)` by declaring this field. It
-- can hold one and pass one, which is exactly what the ceiling exists to make
-- visible, and it is already how the identical capability is treated when it
-- appears in a function signature. Unlike the deserialization hole (Check A),
-- reaching this one needs no unimplemented feature.
--
-- Accept companion: accept/t144, the same declarations under a covering
-- `needs`, which must typecheck AND raise no "declared but never used"
-- warning — these positions count as uses.
mod FieldCap do
  needs IO.Console

  type Handle = { id : Int, tok : Cap(IO.FileWrite) }

  fn main() do
    println("a capability this module never declared")
  end
end
